assed out with an armed 7k guy  standing over her there's definitely  more going on here than what we've seen  but at this point it's hard to pin down  what that is then we have will who we  learned a lot about in some ways but  maybe not the things that we were hoping  to find out a lot of people like the  theory that he could be hooded justice  and it does seem a little bit more  likely after this episode I like the  idea where maybe he was the inspiration  for her to justice or that there was  more than one of them or something along  those lines but but either way American  hero story revealing that hood of  justice wasn't role to Mueller could be  big I'm guessing that will was saved at  the end by Lady trues people but that's  not exactly a slam dunk  I think some people will wonder if maybe  night out was involved in this but that  seems pretty far-fetched the question of  whether he killed the chief or not is  still out there and if he did then why  him being Angela's grandfather could be  important but we also know that she grew  up in Vietnam where something probably  happened to her parents so does any of  what we saw today move us closer to  solving the mystery that he represents I  don't think so  and of course the same goes for the old  lord of the manor  he seems trapped or imprisoned or  something he's got quite a few clones at  his disposal and he really enjoys the  play that he authored about dr.  Manhattan fans are probably thrilled  that they got a blue dong finally here  in this episode but I'm not sure it  explains much about what's going on  there in that part of the world and I'm  not complaining I like building out the  stories of the characters and like  having the mystery stew simmering over  there on the stovetop the Easter eggs  are everywhere and yet they don't seem  obnoxious in a way that they're being  presented there's a ton of good theories  popping up that you can ponder and I'm  not sure I'm married to any of them yet  it's a goo